{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none. The only top-level data variable, `x0`, is a context input used for simulation in `generated quantities` and is not scored by any sampling statement.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required; the program has no model likelihood, no parameters requiring priors, and no protected observations.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  vector[3] x0;
}

transformed data {
  int<lower=0> M = 3;           // Number of covariates
  int<lower=0> N = 100;         // Number of observations

  vector[M] z0 = [3, 1, -2]';
  real gamma0 = 10;               // True intercept
  vector[M] gamma1 = [2, -3, 1]'; // True slopes
  matrix[M, M] gamma2 = [ [0.5, -0.5, -2.0],
                          [-0.5, 0.25, -1.0],
                          [-2.0, -1.0, 1.0] ];
  real sigma = 0.5;              // True measurement variability
}

generated quantities {
  matrix[N, M] X; // Covariate design matrix
  array[N] real y;      // Variates

  for (n in 1:N) {
    X[n, 1] = normal_rng(x0[1], 2);
    X[n, 2] = normal_rng(x0[2] + 3 * cos(X[n, 1] - x0[1]), 1.25);
    X[n, 3] = normal_rng(x0[3] - (X[n, 1] - x0[1]), 1);
    y[n] = normal_rng(  gamma0
                      + (X[n] - z0') * gamma1
                      + (X[n] - z0') * gamma2 * (X[n] - z0')', sigma);
  }
}

